    </section>
    <section class="summary" id="sect-00004">
    <list id="list-00007">
    <item>Happiness in adulthood can be based on both short-term factors, such as enjoyable activities, and longer-term factors, such as financial stability or social support.</item>
    <item>Life satisfaction in adulthood is influenced both by individual factors as well as cultural values. Influences on life satisfaction also change with age.</item>
    <item>Generative priorities can produce happiness derived from a sense of purpose or meaning, but successful growth in adulthood is facilitated by balancing one’s self with the responsibility to care for others.</item>
    <item>Reflection on one’s actual and possible selves can facilitate this balance and healthy development of self.</item>
    </list>
    </section>
